1
00:00:48,990 --> 00:00:52,940
[The Old Story of Yu Hong]

2
00:00:53,510 --> 00:00:55,910
[Episode 29]

3
00:01:07,340 --> 00:01:10,340
Hao Jie is already in Shanghai,
receiving treatment at a hospital.

4
00:01:10,340 --> 00:01:12,270
The doctors there are really good.

5
00:01:12,780 --> 00:01:13,620
Don't worry.

6
00:01:13,760 --> 00:01:15,820
Her illness can definitely be cured.

7
00:01:16,950 --> 00:01:17,420
Here,

8
00:01:18,280 --> 00:01:19,140
eat this apple.

9
00:01:19,530 --> 00:01:20,390
Weiguo,

10
00:01:23,240 --> 00:01:25,150
when are we going to see a movie?

11
00:01:33,620 --> 00:01:34,630
What did you say?

12
00:01:41,090 --> 00:01:42,720
I want to see a movie.

13
00:01:45,750 --> 00:01:46,880
What did you call me?

14
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:26,150
You're back.

15
00:02:52,790 --> 00:02:54,610
I'll pay back that 300,000 yuan.

16
00:02:57,530 --> 00:02:58,870
What do you mean by that?

17
00:03:00,530 --> 00:03:01,560
You think I spent that 300,000 yuan

18
00:03:01,560 --> 00:03:03,210
to buy you away from her?

19
00:03:03,240 --> 00:03:04,840
Take a good look at yourself.

20
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:06,410
Do you really think
you're worth that much?

21
00:03:06,410 --> 00:03:07,560
If you're leaving, then get the hell out.

22
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:10,220
I don't need your 300,000 yuan
for your freedom.

23
00:03:10,490 --> 00:03:11,340
Thanks.

24
00:03:47,079 --> 00:03:48,000
Thank you.

25
00:04:04,300 --> 00:04:05,780
Keep going and we'll be out of the city.

26
00:04:05,780 --> 00:04:07,260
I'm so confused.

27
00:04:07,430 --> 00:04:08,960
Ms. Wan said to head south,

28
00:04:09,060 --> 00:04:10,370
but she never said how far south.

29
00:04:10,370 --> 00:04:11,460
Vietnam is south,

30
00:04:11,460 --> 00:04:12,720
and so is South Africa.

31
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:14,210
We can't just keep going
until we reach the South Pole, can we?

32
00:04:14,210 --> 00:04:15,280
Oh, give me a break.

33
00:04:15,560 --> 00:04:16,690
Vietnam isn't south.

34
00:04:16,690 --> 00:04:17,560
It's over to the west.

35
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:18,329
Quit talking nonsense.

36
00:04:18,329 --> 00:04:19,730
Have you ever read a book?

37
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:21,420
Vietnam is down by Inner Mongolia.

38
00:04:21,420 --> 00:04:22,130
Really?

39
00:04:23,070 --> 00:04:24,930
Then I must've gotten it mixed up.

40
00:04:24,930 --> 00:04:26,190
You're the man.

41
00:04:28,890 --> 00:04:29,510
Oh, right.

42
00:04:30,420 --> 00:04:31,000
A few days ago,

43
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:32,430
a few shop owners found out
Dong had gone missing,

44
00:04:32,430 --> 00:04:34,000
and they stopped paying
their protection fees.

45
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:35,730
I went to Zhang's butcher shop.

46
00:04:35,800 --> 00:04:37,360
The second I walked in,
they glared at me,

47
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:38,630
then grabbed a knife and chased me out.

48
00:04:38,630 --> 00:04:39,450
Let me tell you.

49
00:04:39,450 --> 00:04:41,310
I was thinking about going
to the bathhouse the other day,

50
00:04:41,310 --> 00:04:43,250
but they asked me
for a bath ticket at the entrance.

51
00:04:43,250 --> 00:04:44,240
When Dong was around,

52
00:04:44,240 --> 00:04:46,170
who would've dared give us any lip?

53
00:04:46,180 --> 00:04:46,810
How about

54
00:04:47,220 --> 00:04:48,280
we call the police?

55
00:04:49,190 --> 00:04:50,590
We can't call the police.

56
00:04:54,430 --> 00:04:57,830
Dong has gone into the jaws
of danger to hone himself.

57
00:04:58,360 --> 00:05:01,690
When he comes out, he'll make a name
for himself far and wide.

58
00:05:01,930 --> 00:05:03,680
He's off doing something big.

59
00:05:04,220 --> 00:05:05,040
Calling the police now

60
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:06,970
would interrupt his cultivation.

61
00:05:07,570 --> 00:05:08,500
And that would make you...

62
00:05:08,500 --> 00:05:09,420
A traitor!

63
00:05:09,420 --> 00:05:11,190
You're the man.

64
00:05:12,120 --> 00:05:14,570
When it matters most, you find out
who's loyal and who's not.

65
00:05:14,570 --> 00:05:16,070
You can tell who's a true brother

66
00:05:16,070 --> 00:05:17,910
by how he acts now.

67
00:05:19,070 --> 00:05:19,770
hat are you doing?

68
00:05:19,340 --> 00:05:19,970
[Yuhong Square Police Station]

69
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:23,330
Officer Ma.

70
00:05:23,950 --> 00:05:24,720
What time is it?

71
00:05:24,660 --> 00:05:25,720
[Yuhong Square Police Station]

72
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:25,550
Hurry home.

73
00:05:26,100 --> 00:05:27,300
All right, all right.

74
00:05:28,810 --> 00:05:29,750
[Golden Imperial Dance Hall]

75
00:05:31,500 --> 00:05:32,980
[Golden Imperial Dance Hall]

76
00:05:33,190 --> 00:05:35,650
The last time Dong called me
into his office,

77
00:05:36,830 --> 00:05:38,390
he put his hand on my shoulder

78
00:05:38,390 --> 00:05:40,180
and said to me earnestly,

79
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:41,890
"Man,

80
00:05:42,950 --> 00:05:45,060
this time, you've got a big job to do."

81
00:05:47,250 --> 00:05:47,750
Then...

82
00:05:48,950 --> 00:05:50,000
what was it?

83
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:54,870
What's this?

84
00:05:56,870 --> 00:05:58,770
Your sideburns?

85
00:06:00,690 --> 00:06:01,620
Brain.

86
00:06:03,370 --> 00:06:04,360
Dong said

87
00:06:04,450 --> 00:06:07,800
we need to use our brains
when we're doing things.

88
00:06:12,410 --> 00:06:13,140
Right.

89
00:06:13,740 --> 00:06:14,860
Dong did say

90
00:06:14,880 --> 00:06:16,240
we had a big job to do.

91
00:06:16,430 --> 00:06:17,720
But the last time I asked him
what it was,

92
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:19,580
he... he wouldn't tell me either.

93
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:21,660
Do you remember?

94
00:06:21,750 --> 00:06:23,670
There was this one time
Dong said he was going to meet someone,

95
00:06:23,670 --> 00:06:25,530
and he wouldn't let us come along.

96
00:06:26,740 --> 00:06:27,540
That's right.

97
00:06:27,540 --> 00:06:29,180
San Yan'er's brother-in-law has a sister.

98
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:30,000
Dong even had me

99
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:31,840
look into her a while back.

100
00:06:32,170 --> 00:06:33,380
He said she's a cop
and that we should get to know her,

101
00:06:33,380 --> 00:06:35,380
build a good relationship with her.

102
00:06:37,390 --> 00:06:38,320
I get it now.

103
00:06:38,790 --> 00:06:40,420
Dong must've been sent by the police

104
00:06:40,420 --> 00:06:42,020
to go undercover.

105
00:06:47,510 --> 00:06:49,090
Usually, when I go out
to stock up on cigarettes,

106
00:06:49,090 --> 00:06:50,840
he only sends me away for a day or two.

107
00:06:50,840 --> 00:06:51,770
This time, he sent me to Guangzhou

108
00:06:51,770 --> 00:06:53,870
for so long

109
00:06:55,300 --> 00:06:57,000
so I could learn

110
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:00,120
from the KTVs there.

111
00:07:02,270 --> 00:07:04,060
We can't let Dong down.

112
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:09,160
If Dong really did go undercover,

113
00:07:10,270 --> 00:07:11,330
then we really ought

114
00:07:11,330 --> 00:07:13,660
to start doing some legitimate business.

115
00:07:14,980 --> 00:07:16,780
You're the one who gets it, Meng.

116
00:07:16,870 --> 00:07:17,950
Dong said

117
00:07:18,450 --> 00:07:19,850
we need to use our brains.

118
00:07:25,950 --> 00:07:28,040
Karaoke halls in Guangzhou
aren't called dance halls.

119
00:07:27,860 --> 00:07:28,830
[Responsible Entertainment,
Worry-Free Singing]

120
00:07:28,040 --> 00:07:29,180
They're called KTVs.

121
00:07:28,880 --> 00:07:29,740
[Say No to Vice, Keep Our Karaoke Clean]

122
00:07:29,420 --> 00:07:31,560
You don't hug and cuddle
on the dance floor,

123
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:31,810
[Stay Clean, Sing Healthy,
Promote a Better Culture]

124
00:07:31,560 --> 00:07:32,800
and you don't have to wait
to request a song.

125
00:07:31,890 --> 00:07:32,720
[Welcome]
[Come Sing Out on a Night in Tiecheng]

126
00:07:32,840 --> 00:07:33,470
[A Huge Selection of Hits, Sing What You Like]
[Drinks & Snacks, Perfect for Casual Gatherings]

127
00:07:32,890 --> 00:07:34,370
They're all private rooms—

128
00:07:33,540 --> 00:07:34,300
[20% Off All Drinks] [Set A: 58]

129
00:07:34,500 --> 00:07:37,500
separate, discreet, and civilized.

130
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:39,650
That's what a proper KTV should be like.

131
00:07:39,650 --> 00:07:41,180
Throw out all those fake cigarettes
and fake liquor.

132
00:07:41,180 --> 00:07:42,310
Don't keep any of it.

133
00:07:42,420 --> 00:07:44,330
From now on, we only sell cigarettes
and liquor from legitimate sources.

134
00:07:44,330 --> 00:07:45,140
Even if the Industry and Commerce Bureau
comes to inspect us,

135
00:07:45,140 --> 00:07:46,180
we've got nothing to worry about.

136
00:07:46,180 --> 00:07:47,740
We're not in this for a quick buck.

137
00:07:47,740 --> 00:07:50,140
We've got to think long-term, understand?

138
00:07:50,159 --> 00:07:51,390
And the staff there

139
00:07:51,390 --> 00:07:52,500
aren't like ours.

140
00:07:52,659 --> 00:07:53,370
Just look at

141
00:07:53,370 --> 00:07:54,770
what our staff are like.

142
00:07:54,770 --> 00:07:55,570
From now on, our staff

143
00:07:55,570 --> 00:07:57,450
have to be professional
and follow standardized procedures.

144
00:07:57,450 --> 00:07:58,370
Things can't be like they used to be.

145
00:07:58,370 --> 00:07:59,890
-Did you get a nose job, sis?
-No, I didn't.

146
00:07:59,890 --> 00:08:01,290
You look different to me.

147
00:08:01,300 --> 00:08:02,530
I haven't changed.

148
00:08:02,620 --> 00:08:03,270
Don't be ridiculous.

149
00:08:03,270 --> 00:08:05,400
Why are you still hanging around here?

150
00:08:05,830 --> 00:08:07,830
From now on, we're done holding hands,

151
00:08:07,830 --> 00:08:09,390
kissing guests, letting them
touch our thighs, and all that.

152
00:08:09,390 --> 00:08:11,190
If we can't kiss them, what can we do?

153
00:08:11,190 --> 00:08:12,100
-Exactly.
-Exactly.

154
00:08:12,100 --> 00:08:13,360
-Why can't we kiss anymore?
-Seriously.

155
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:14,120
Why?

156
00:08:14,120 --> 00:08:15,240
Yun, didn't I tell you

157
00:08:15,240 --> 00:08:16,660
there's a chant?
You're supposed to teach them.

158
00:08:16,660 --> 00:08:17,010
-What chant?
-What chant?

159
00:08:17,010 --> 00:08:18,040
What chant?

160
00:08:18,430 --> 00:08:19,480
Come on, Yun. Show them how it's done.

161
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:20,390
What chant?
Did all that teaching go to waste?

162
00:08:20,390 --> 00:08:21,100
Get down here.

163
00:08:21,100 --> 00:08:21,570
Show some decorum.

164
00:08:21,570 --> 00:08:22,680
The leader is right here.

165
00:08:22,680 --> 00:08:23,680
Come on, hurry up.

166
00:08:24,040 --> 00:08:24,930
Loud and clear, okay? Raise your voice.

167
00:08:24,930 --> 00:08:25,560
Okay.

168
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:27,240
One, two, three.

169
00:08:27,240 --> 00:08:29,330
-Welcome!
-Welcome!

170
00:08:35,770 --> 00:08:36,570
What's wrong?

171
00:08:36,840 --> 00:08:38,240
Why isn't he saying anything?

172
00:08:38,240 --> 00:08:39,169
What's going on?

173
00:08:39,360 --> 00:08:40,580
-Where is he going?
-Why is he leaving?

174
00:08:40,580 --> 00:08:41,409
What's wrong with him?

175
00:08:41,409 --> 00:08:42,080
What happened?

176
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:44,650
[May Buddha's Light Shine Upon You
and Bring Prosperity to Your Business]

177
00:08:44,690 --> 00:08:48,260
[Golden Imperial Dance Hall]

178
00:08:48,280 --> 00:08:52,940
[Grand Opening! Everyone Is Welcome]

179
00:08:49,440 --> 00:08:50,410
Ms. Wan said

180
00:08:50,410 --> 00:08:53,210
11:00 is the auspicious time
to open for business.

181
00:08:54,120 --> 00:08:55,410
My watch has stopped.

182
00:08:56,080 --> 00:08:57,810
Do you guys know what time it is?

183
00:09:00,670 --> 00:09:01,440
What time is it?

184
00:09:01,440 --> 00:09:03,120
Mine says 11:05.

185
00:09:03,120 --> 00:09:03,790
Oh, give me a break.

186
00:09:03,790 --> 00:09:05,000
Mine says 10:50.

187
00:09:05,510 --> 00:09:07,000
Why does mine say 12:00?

188
00:09:07,620 --> 00:09:09,420
Is yours keeping accurate time?

189
00:09:09,740 --> 00:09:10,860
Mine runs a little slow.

190
00:09:10,860 --> 00:09:12,720
Then won't that make you an idiot?

191
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:15,850
Meng, do you know what time it is?

192
00:09:18,480 --> 00:09:19,390
Around noon.

193
00:09:22,660 --> 00:09:24,190
So, are we doing this or not?

194
00:09:24,240 --> 00:09:24,890
Hurry up.

195
00:09:26,050 --> 00:09:27,790
[Golden Imperial Dance Hall]

196
00:09:26,510 --> 00:09:27,170
You scared me.

197
00:09:27,170 --> 00:09:28,700
Are you an idiot?

198
00:09:27,810 --> 00:09:30,190
[Grand Opening! Everyone Is Welcome]

199
00:09:29,220 --> 00:09:30,050
Let's do one.

200
00:09:33,410 --> 00:09:35,910
If we're doing it,
shouldn't we all do it together?

201
00:09:35,910 --> 00:09:36,550
You...

202
00:09:37,080 --> 00:09:37,600
You're unbelievable.

203
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:37,870
All right,

204
00:09:37,870 --> 00:09:38,440
we're done here, right?

205
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:39,670
Let's finish up and head back.

206
00:09:39,670 --> 00:09:41,080
I'm freezing my ass off here.

207
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:41,960
Let's go. Let's go.

208
00:09:41,140 --> 00:09:44,170
[Grand Opening! Everyone Is Welcome]

209
00:09:47,630 --> 00:09:49,290
This is a tough crew to manage.

210
00:10:03,290 --> 00:10:08,060
[Golden Imperial Dance Hall—Grand Opening]

211
00:10:37,410 --> 00:10:40,270
That little belly of yours
is getting pretty round.

212
00:10:44,870 --> 00:10:45,930
Why are these pants

213
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:47,830
so short?

214
00:10:48,200 --> 00:10:49,390
Did they shrink?

215
00:10:50,200 --> 00:10:51,010
No way.

216
00:10:51,010 --> 00:10:52,340
Didn't we just buy them?

217
00:10:52,700 --> 00:10:54,500
How did they get so much shorter?

218
00:10:58,580 --> 00:11:01,840
These shoes are uncomfortable.
They're pinching my toes.

219
00:11:14,630 --> 00:11:18,090
If they're pinching your toes,
don't wear these for now. Here,

220
00:11:19,510 --> 00:11:20,440
step into these.

221
00:11:21,300 --> 00:11:23,630
These are a little tight too, aren't they?

222
00:11:24,120 --> 00:11:26,580
Let me see how tall you've gotten.
Come here.

223
00:11:27,370 --> 00:11:28,370
Let me take a look.

224
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:31,320
Stand up straight.

225
00:11:36,080 --> 00:11:37,440
You've grown so much!

226
00:11:54,500 --> 00:11:55,830
Of course you've grown.

227
00:11:56,900 --> 00:11:58,500
You've been here for so long.

228
00:12:01,240 --> 00:12:01,770
Let's go.

229
00:12:02,120 --> 00:12:04,260
I'll take you shoe shopping, okay?

230
00:12:05,010 --> 00:12:07,540
We'll get you
some new clothes and pants, too.

231
00:12:09,990 --> 00:12:12,110
Here, let me wrap this little scarf
around you.

232
00:12:12,110 --> 00:12:14,110
This little vest is pretty nice too.

233
00:12:14,530 --> 00:12:15,990
Let's get the shoes first.

234
00:12:16,100 --> 00:12:18,030
Your feet are growing way too fast.

235
00:12:18,980 --> 00:12:21,240
Here, take a look. See which one you like.

236
00:12:21,250 --> 00:12:21,870
This one.

237
00:12:22,650 --> 00:12:23,470
This one?

238
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:24,860
Good choice.

239
00:12:25,130 --> 00:12:26,010
Do you have this in a size 27?

240
00:12:26,010 --> 00:12:27,010
Yes, this is the one.

241
00:12:27,010 --> 00:12:27,790
Then bring me both. Let's try them on.

242
00:12:27,790 --> 00:12:28,770
Come on, try them on.

243
00:12:28,770 --> 00:12:29,440
Sit here.

244
00:12:38,250 --> 00:12:43,180
[Lisiman Bedding]

245
00:12:38,770 --> 00:12:40,170
This one is pretty good.

246
00:12:40,580 --> 00:12:41,510
No, this one won't do.

247
00:12:41,510 --> 00:12:43,460
Turn around and look
at the one behind you.

248
00:12:43,460 --> 00:12:44,520
That one's higher.

249
00:12:44,870 --> 00:12:48,470
It's easier on your back when you're
holding the baby. You get it?

250
00:12:48,480 --> 00:12:51,210
Yeah, that one's quite a bit higher
than this one.

251
00:12:52,550 --> 00:12:53,200
Liu Yang,

252
00:12:54,290 --> 00:12:55,290
give me a hand.

253
00:12:59,850 --> 00:13:02,270
[Watch Your Step]

254
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:02,100
Let's go over there
and have a look

255
00:13:02,620 --> 00:13:04,150
at those small mattresses.

256
00:13:17,340 --> 00:13:18,200
The cornflakes—

257
00:13:18,200 --> 00:13:19,250
kids actually like those.

258
00:13:19,250 --> 00:13:20,460
Move it closer to her.

259
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:22,700
It's fine.
You don't have to worry about her.

260
00:13:22,700 --> 00:13:23,150
It's fine.

261
00:13:23,150 --> 00:13:25,750
I'm afraid the fried one
might prick her mouth.

262
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:28,010
Want some juice?

263
00:13:28,720 --> 00:13:29,370
Have some juice.

264
00:13:29,370 --> 00:13:30,770
Pineapple juice is fine.

265
00:13:30,840 --> 00:13:32,440
She just loves sweet things.

266
00:13:32,700 --> 00:13:34,260
All kids love sweet things.

267
00:13:34,510 --> 00:13:36,110
-Have a bite.
-Isn't it good?

268
00:13:36,510 --> 00:13:38,650
What's gotten into you today?
Getting all shy?

269
00:13:38,650 --> 00:13:39,650
The cake's here.

270
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:41,810
This is too much. You shouldn't
have gone to all this trouble.

271
00:13:41,810 --> 00:13:43,610
Just eat as much as you can, Juan.

272
00:13:44,650 --> 00:13:46,650
The dessert came out a little early.

273
00:13:48,740 --> 00:13:50,370
Cake—Qianqian likes cake, right?

274
00:13:50,370 --> 00:13:51,010
She does.

275
00:13:51,010 --> 00:13:52,340
She loves sweet things.

276
00:13:52,500 --> 00:13:52,960
Come on,

277
00:13:53,370 --> 00:13:54,980
that's enough. Quit pretending and eat.

278
00:13:54,980 --> 00:13:55,200
Come on.

279
00:13:55,200 --> 00:13:56,080
Give it a try.

280
00:13:56,740 --> 00:13:57,870
What's wrong today?

281
00:13:58,460 --> 00:13:59,970
Not much of an appetite.

282
00:14:00,750 --> 00:14:01,500
I'll eat it.

283
00:14:02,580 --> 00:14:04,580
M-Maybe she doesn't like the taste.

284
00:14:04,630 --> 00:14:05,460
She's just a little shy.

285
00:14:05,460 --> 00:14:06,820
She's like this whenever
there are a lot of people around.

286
00:14:06,820 --> 00:14:07,480
I'll eat it.

287
00:14:09,320 --> 00:14:10,130
Is it okay?

288
00:14:10,130 --> 00:14:11,840
It's good, it's good, it's good.

289
00:14:11,840 --> 00:14:12,900
It's a little cold.

290
00:14:15,890 --> 00:14:17,350
I'm going to the bathroom.

291
00:14:17,720 --> 00:14:19,080
-I-I'll go with you.
-Keep eating. Don't wait for me.

292
00:14:19,080 --> 00:14:19,530
I'll go with you.

293
00:14:19,530 --> 00:14:21,340
It's fine. You don't have to. Sit down.

294
00:14:21,340 --> 00:14:21,770
Sit down. Sit down.

295
00:14:21,770 --> 00:14:22,600
Be careful.

296
00:14:31,790 --> 00:14:34,050
All right, quit pretending and drink up.

297
00:14:40,150 --> 00:14:41,880
She's had it pretty rough, too.

298
00:14:47,600 --> 00:14:48,580
Has Hao Jie

299
00:14:48,820 --> 00:14:50,130
not been in touch lately?

300
00:14:50,130 --> 00:14:50,700
No.

301
00:14:58,440 --> 00:15:00,100
None of you men are any good.

302
00:15:05,630 --> 00:15:07,750
Qianqian, eat up. Here.

303
00:15:14,870 --> 00:15:15,840
You were little back then.

304
00:15:15,840 --> 00:15:16,970
You don't remember.

305
00:15:17,750 --> 00:15:20,010
Mom would cry her eyes out all night,

306
00:15:21,200 --> 00:15:22,550
while Dad wouldn't say a word.

307
00:15:22,550 --> 00:15:24,910
He'd just stay
on the balcony, chain-smoking.

308
00:15:24,910 --> 00:15:26,680
Eventually, everyone in the neighborhood
started talking,

309
00:15:26,680 --> 00:15:28,140
and that's when I found out

310
00:15:28,560 --> 00:15:30,150
Dad was cheating on Mom.

311
00:15:32,010 --> 00:15:33,740
I don't know that woman's name,

312
00:15:34,450 --> 00:15:35,910
but I've always hated her.

313
00:15:39,630 --> 00:15:40,270
Later,

314
00:15:42,550 --> 00:15:43,560
later, when Sun Zheng

315
00:15:43,560 --> 00:15:44,760
went to Guangzhou...

316
00:15:45,150 --> 00:15:45,790
I finally

317
00:15:46,270 --> 00:15:47,800
saw you men for what you are.

318
00:15:48,130 --> 00:15:48,720
You men are
all a bunch of heartless bastards

319
00:15:48,720 --> 00:15:51,320
who get tired of the old
and want something new.

320
00:15:57,390 --> 00:15:58,010
Juan,

321
00:15:59,130 --> 00:16:01,170
it really was my fault that Hao Jie and I

322
00:16:01,170 --> 00:16:02,570
couldn't stay together.

323
00:16:02,820 --> 00:16:04,510
I'm not even myself anymore.

324
00:16:05,940 --> 00:16:07,070
I don't get to decide

325
00:16:07,370 --> 00:16:08,370
what I've become.

326
00:16:14,770 --> 00:16:16,370
What are you babbling about?

327
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:19,930
Why are you getting all weird, too?

328
00:16:20,510 --> 00:16:22,570
What nonsense are you talking about?

329
00:16:30,740 --> 00:16:31,750
Why haven't you eaten much?

330
00:16:31,750 --> 00:16:32,840
We did eat. We did.

331
00:16:32,840 --> 00:16:33,580
We were waiting for you.

332
00:16:33,580 --> 00:16:35,270
Don't wait for me. The kid's hungry.

333
00:16:35,270 --> 00:16:36,250
It's fine. Don't worry about her.

334
00:16:36,250 --> 00:16:37,510
I don't know
what's gotten into her today.

335
00:16:37,510 --> 00:16:38,320
She's just sitting here
like she's been glued to her seat.

336
00:16:38,320 --> 00:16:39,170
You eat first. You eat first.

337
00:16:39,170 --> 00:16:40,250
Okay, okay, okay.

338
00:16:40,250 --> 00:16:40,910
Are you okay?

339
00:16:40,910 --> 00:16:41,870
I'm fine. I just

340
00:16:42,370 --> 00:16:43,790
drank too much water before we left.

341
00:16:43,790 --> 00:16:44,500
It's fine, it's fine.

342
00:16:44,500 --> 00:16:45,410
Eat. Eat.

343
00:16:46,120 --> 00:16:48,250
If you don't like it, just give it to me.

344
00:16:48,440 --> 00:16:49,010
Is it good?

345
00:16:49,010 --> 00:16:49,940
Okay. It's good.

346
00:16:50,150 --> 00:16:51,840
You left the house
without even fixing your collar.

347
00:16:51,840 --> 00:16:52,940
What a goof.

348
00:16:58,840 --> 00:16:59,870
Hey,

349
00:17:00,170 --> 00:17:01,910
where are you?

350
00:17:03,790 --> 00:17:06,540
Did you get some fries?

351
00:17:07,829 --> 00:17:10,050
Where are you now?

352
00:17:13,310 --> 00:17:14,010
Well, look

353
00:17:14,010 --> 00:17:15,700
who finally crawled out of the grave.

354
00:17:15,700 --> 00:17:16,810
After all this time,

355
00:17:16,810 --> 00:17:17,380
you finally remembered

356
00:17:17,380 --> 00:17:18,880
you have a daughter of your own.

357
00:17:18,880 --> 00:17:19,530
What,

358
00:17:19,700 --> 00:17:21,400
you finally topped up your phone?

359
00:17:21,400 --> 00:17:23,349
Your daughter has been here
with me all this time,

360
00:17:23,349 --> 00:17:25,030
and you've been completely out of touch.

361
00:17:25,030 --> 00:17:26,940
You think you're some kind
of baby-delivering Bodhisattva?

362
00:17:26,940 --> 00:17:28,569
When she asks me who her father is,

363
00:17:28,569 --> 00:17:30,050
I'll tell her it was a mantis.

364
00:17:30,050 --> 00:17:31,030
After he fathered her,

365
00:17:31,030 --> 00:17:32,980
the female mantis ate him.

366
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:35,660
Juan,

367
00:17:35,880 --> 00:17:37,250
it's me, He Liang.

368
00:17:41,260 --> 00:17:43,190
How many times have you two talked?

369
00:17:43,640 --> 00:17:44,680
I had no idea.

370
00:17:45,200 --> 00:17:46,960
Qianqian's got a good memory.

371
00:17:46,960 --> 00:17:48,530
She memorized my phone number

372
00:17:48,530 --> 00:17:50,500
and likes to call me and chat in dialect
whenever she's got nothing to do.

373
00:17:50,500 --> 00:17:51,660
That's her dialect,

374
00:17:51,660 --> 00:17:52,980
not yours.

375
00:17:53,200 --> 00:17:54,250
Aren't you basically just using her

376
00:17:54,250 --> 00:17:55,740
as a language-learning tool?

377
00:17:55,740 --> 00:17:57,880
We're learning from each other.

378
00:17:58,250 --> 00:17:59,050
You...

379
00:17:59,160 --> 00:18:01,490
Have you learned a few Cantonese phrases?

380
00:18:02,400 --> 00:18:03,800
I don't speak Cantonese.

381
00:18:04,330 --> 00:18:06,090
I only know those two lines from the song.

382
00:18:06,090 --> 00:18:06,810
What song?

383
00:18:07,310 --> 00:18:08,110
Sing it for me.

384
00:18:14,420 --> 00:18:16,480
The one on your tape recorder.

385
00:18:17,710 --> 00:18:20,400
♪ Cold and warm, when can they rest? ♪

386
00:18:20,660 --> 00:18:23,880
♪ Looking back, how many autumns? ♪

387
00:18:24,060 --> 00:18:24,980
All right,

388
00:18:25,330 --> 00:18:26,290
I don't sing very well.

389
00:18:26,290 --> 00:18:27,270
You sing great.

390
00:18:27,610 --> 00:18:28,910
That's impressive.

391
00:18:29,050 --> 00:18:30,110
Oh, stop it.

392
00:18:30,110 --> 00:18:31,960
I don't even know what the lyrics mean.

393
00:18:31,960 --> 00:18:32,700
It's good.

394
00:18:33,460 --> 00:18:35,260
Has Qianqian gotten any taller?

395
00:18:35,270 --> 00:18:36,660
I don't see much of a difference.

396
00:18:36,660 --> 00:18:38,110
She still looks about the same size.

397
00:18:38,110 --> 00:18:39,240
Have you gotten any taller?

398
00:18:39,240 --> 00:18:40,330
How could I still be growing?

399
00:18:40,330 --> 00:18:41,480
Look how old I am.

400
00:18:41,920 --> 00:18:44,380
If I got any taller,
I'd turn into a giantess.

401
00:18:45,550 --> 00:18:46,960
How's work been lately?

402
00:18:47,590 --> 00:18:48,550
Same as always.

403
00:18:48,790 --> 00:18:50,330
Don't force yourself
to make conversation.

404
00:18:50,330 --> 00:18:52,000
Have you run out of things to say?

405
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:54,800
I just wanted to chat with you.
